Z||000000||BN Boomer||04-04-2000||12:52 AM||||I just bought an 85 GT for a good price due to the problem that the engine was making funny noises and now will turn over but not start. I have already replaced the ignition module, pickup coil, and ignition coil. A good spark is produced. I have also disconnected the tach filter to no avail. I know it's getting fuel because I can smell it after trying to start it for a while. The engine sounds like it is about to catch but won't run on it's own. I've also tried fiddling with the timing a bit but that didn't help, either.<P>I should also note that the seller said the engine was making a tapping sound like a stuck lifter when it ran previously. He said he drove the car back and forth to the end of his driveway each day to show it for sale and one day it just quit running and wouldn't start again. He claimed there was no big bang or anything and I can't hear any grotesque noises when the engine is cranking over. I also got an additional supposedly good running V-6 out of another 85 Fiero with this car, but I would like to at least know that everything else is in working order before starting to mess around with an engine swap. I would really like to get this motor in decent working order and do a performance rebuild on the other, or maybe vice-versa if this engine proves too mechanically far gone to repair in the car.<P>Any other ideas or suggestions on what to look for? This one's got me scratching my head!||||reg||8
